  "instructions": [
    "Heat the olive oil in the ttukbaegi earthenware over medium heat.",
    "Add the diced onion and sauté until translucent, about 3-4 minutes.",
    "Add the minced garlic and sauté for another minute.",
    "Add the dried thyme, ground cumin, salt, and black pepper. Stir well.",
    "Add the Greek bean sprouts and stir to combine with the spice mixture.",
    "Place the banana leaves on top of the bean sprouts and cover the ttukbaegi earthenware.",
    "Steam the contents over low heat for 20-25 minutes, or until the bean sprouts are tender.",
    "Remove the banana leaves and garnish with chopped fresh parsley and raisins, if using.",
    "Serve hot, directly from the ttukbaegi earthenware."
